# Build artifacts
build/
src/build/
build-cov/
*.o
*.d

# Per-binary gcov payloads, written into the repository root by the coverage
# script and cleaned by `make coverage-clean`.
*.gcov.json.gz

# Generated by the build into the repository root (templates in scripts/)
/ktplace.sh
/ktplace.csh

# Generated placements and plots
output/
# ...except the ISPD 2005 suite driver, which is the regression entry point and
# refers to the vendored adaptec1, so it belongs next to it rather than only on
# whoever's machine happens to have written it.
!output/
output/*
!output/run_ispd2005.sh
out.pl

# Run transcript
ktplace.log
*.log

# Benchmark data is downloaded, not committed: keep the directory itself
# visible so the fetch script and its docs can be tracked.
benchmark/*
!benchmark/fetch_benchmarks.py
!benchmark/README.md

# adaptec1 is the exception, and it is deliberate. It is the CI smoke design, and
# the ISPD 2005 suite has no download URL that still works -- the UMich mirror
# 404s and the UT Austin tarball 403s -- so a job that has to fetch it would just
# be a red build waiting to happen. The suite is redistributed by dozens of
# placement papers without a canonical home, and the whole design is 5.4 MB
# already gzipped, which is a fair price for a smoke test that cannot break on
# someone else's uptime. Only this one design is tracked; the other seven stay
# ignored, and `output/run_ispd2005.sh` skips any design it cannot find.
!benchmark/ISPD_2005/
benchmark/ISPD_2005/*
!benchmark/ISPD_2005/adaptec1/

# Editor / OS noise
*.swp
.DS_Store
.claude
.opencode
logs/

# Local editor tooling (kept out of the repo)
.cursorrules
# Development notes are ignored; the curated write-ups are tracked.
docs/*
!docs/simpl.md
ref/
*.whl

# Downloaded toolchain (Doxygen), same policy as the benchmark data: fetched, not
# committed. `make docs` fetches it.
tools/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# clangd compilation database: regenerated by `make compile-commands`.
# The include paths are absolute, so a committed copy is wrong elsewhere, and a
# stale one makes clangd report diagnostics from flags the build does not use.
compile_commands.json
